<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Industry_Retail> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Industry> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT010> <https://example.org/sales-kg/identifier> "ACT010" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT001> <https://example.org/sales-kg/hasParticipant> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Contact_C001> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT001> <https://example.org/sales-kg/transcriptText> "Anna said the solution fits their operational goals, but asked for a stronger volume discount if they expand to three factories." .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT003> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Interaction> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Contact_C007> <https://example.org/sales-kg/name> "Camille Martin" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_T004> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Transcript> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D009> <https://example.org/sales-kg/involvesProduct> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Product_AI%20Add-on> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT001> <https://example.org/sales-kg/interactionDate> "2026-08-28T10:00:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT027> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Transcript> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Contact_C013> <https://example.org/sales-kg/identifier> "C013" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT002> <https://example.org/sales-kg/hasParticipant> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Contact_C002> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Contact_C003> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/CustomerContact> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D010> <https://example.org/sales-kg/winProbability> "0.72"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT027> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Interaction> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT012> <https://example.org/sales-kg/hasParticipant> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Contact_C007> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D004> <https://example.org/sales-kg/identifier> "D004" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_T002> <https://example.org/sales-kg/transcriptText> "Michael (Sales): What would make this pilot successful for you?\nEva de Vries: Forecast accuracy is the main thing. Our managers don't trust the current forecast.\nTom Smit: We also have a lot of custom opportunity fields in the CRM. If your connector ignores those, the dashboard won't be useful.\nMichael: We can map custom fields. Would you be comfortable defining three or four success metrics before the pilot starts?\nEva de Vries: Yes. Forecast accuracy, pipeline coverage, conversion by stage, and probably manager adoption.\nMichael: And if the pilot improves those metrics?\nEva de Vries: Then I can make the case for rolling it out to the entire sales organization." .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT018> <https://example.org/sales-kg/identifier> "ACT018_transcript" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT008> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Transcript> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT005> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Transcript> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_T006> <https://example.org/sales-kg/transcriptText> "Chris (Sales): You mentioned automation is a priority. Which process causes the most pain today?\nLouise Dubois: That's actually what we're still trying to determine. There are many manual processes.\nArthur Peeters: Shipment exception handling is probably the best candidate. The team spends hours coordinating exceptions by email.\nChris: Who owns that process?\nArthur Peeters: Operations, but we should bring the regional operations manager into the next meeting.\nLouise Dubois: Before we discuss software, I want a clear business case around one process.\nChris: Understood. We'll focus the next workshop on shipment exceptions and quantify the current manual effort." .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT017> <https://example.org/sales-kg/transcriptText> "Arthur suggested starting with shipment exception handling because the team currently manages it manually." .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Contact_C016> <https://example.org/sales-kg/identifier> "C016" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D004> <https://example.org/sales-kg/name> "RetailPro Analytics Upgrade" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D008> <https://example.org/sales-kg/involvesProduct> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Product_Starter%20Package> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT017> <https://example.org/sales-kg/identifier> "ACT017" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_T004> <https://example.org/sales-kg/aboutDeal> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D004> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT010> <https://example.org/sales-kg/transcriptText> "Camille liked the capabilities but said the project needs a stronger ROI case to compete with other internal investments." .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT012> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Interaction> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Interaction> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Contact_C009> <https://example.org/sales-kg/decisionMakerFor> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D011> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT024> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Interaction> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D011> <https://example.org/sales-kg/identifier> "D011" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Contact_C007> <https://example.org/sales-kg/decisionMakerFor> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D004> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT008> <https://example.org/sales-kg/hasTranscript> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT008> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT028> <https://example.org/sales-kg/identifier> "ACT028" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT018> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Transcript> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_T007> <https://example.org/sales-kg/transcriptText> "Emma (Sales): Are there any remaining concerns besides commercial terms?\nJames Carter: Model governance is mostly resolved. The documentation Priya reviewed was sufficient.\nPriya Shah: Yes. We still want lineage and monitoring included in the implementation plan, but I don't see that as a blocker.\nEmma: On pricing, what would make a multi-year commitment work?\nJames Carter: The current price is acceptable for one year. For three years, I need a meaningful incentive.\nEmma: Would a lower effective annual price plus price protection address that?\nJames Carter: Potentially. Show me both a two-year and a three-year option.\nEmma: If one of those works commercially, are we ready for legal review?\nJames Carter: Yes." .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D001> <https://example.org/sales-kg/dealStage> "Negotiation" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Contact_C006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/CustomerContact> .
