<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D008> <https://example.org/sales-kg/forAccount> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Account_A008> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT031> <https://example.org/sales-kg/transcriptText> "Louise said other transformation programs have priority and she cannot sponsor the initiative this year." .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT025> <https://example.org/sales-kg/aboutDeal> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D009> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_T003> <https://example.org/sales-kg/transcriptText> "Rachel (Sales): Before we finalize the proposal, are there any technical blockers left?\nMette Nielsen: The architecture looks fine now. My concern was whether you could integrate without creating another isolated data store.\nRachel: The design uses your existing platform and keeps the source systems authoritative.\nMette Nielsen: That's what we needed.\nLars Jensen: For me the bigger question is rollout. I don't want this to become a one-business-unit experiment.\nRachel: We can structure the contract around a phased rollout, but price it as an enterprise agreement.\nLars Jensen: Good. If security signs off and the rollout plan is included, I think we can move forward.\nMette Nielsen: From the technical side, I can recommend approval." .
