<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_T010> <https://example.org/sales-kg/transcriptText> "Chris (Sales): Arthur has been positive about the platform, but he mentioned sponsorship might be an issue.\nLouise Dubois: That's correct. I like the concept, but we have two transformation programs that already have executive backing.\nChris: Is there a smaller scope that you could sponsor?\nLouise Dubois: Not this year. It's less about scope and more about organizational priority.\nArthur Peeters: Could we keep the technical work alive and revisit budget later?\nLouise Dubois: We can revisit it next planning cycle, but I don't want the team spending more time on it now.\nChris: Understood. We'll close the opportunity for now and reconnect during planning." .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_T006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/sales-kg/Transcript> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D003> <https://example.org/sales-kg/name> "GreenEnergy Platform Rollout" .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D001> <https://example.org/sales-kg/involvesProduct> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Product_Enterprise%20Platform> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Deal_D005> <https://example.org/sales-kg/involvesProduct> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Product_Data%20Platform> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Interaction_ACT014> <https://example.org/sales-kg/hasTranscript> <https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_ACT014> .
<https://example.org/sales-kg/resource/Transcript_T004> <https://example.org/sales-kg/transcriptText> "Daniel (Sales): The team seemed positive about the solution. What's stopping the project?\nCamille Martin: The product isn't the issue. Finance froze most discretionary spending for the rest of the year.\nDaniel: Would reducing the project scope help?\nCamille Martin: Probably not. The bigger problem is that this isn't considered critical compared with our other initiatives.\nDaniel: Is there anything we could provide to strengthen the case?\nCamille Martin: A stronger ROI model would help next time, but it won't unlock budget this year.\nDaniel: Should we revisit it during next year's planning cycle?\nCamille Martin: Yes. Contact me around October when we start planning next year's budget." .
